legacy_coverage_note:
The Uniswap Protocol smart contracts on Ethereum remained reachable;
Uniswap Labs' own post distinguishes its control over the app from
the decentralized protocol. No consensus-layer restriction is claimed.

Bitcoin native asset has no issuer-side blacklist/freeze admin method;
USDT first issued ~2014-10 (postdates this event). not_applicable on
construct-did-not-exist grounds.

INR off-ramp severance is recorded under the parent FIU-IND event;
this Apple-action sibling event does not re-record the offramp axis
to avoid double-counting.

No issuer-level asset freeze invoked by Etherscan's UI label;
sibling asset-layer action is captured in
circle-usdc-tornado-2022.

No operator-controlled UI surface is the target of the order;
the seizure order acts directly on address-level custody claims
via Israeli administrative law, not on a frontend.

The five assets are independent base-chain tokens (no issuer/contract);
OKEx cannot freeze them on-chain. The action is an off-ramp market
removal, not an asset-onchain freeze.

No SDN listing or stablecoin-issuer freeze primitive applicable;
CSA's stablecoin-offering restriction operates at the platform-
registration layer, not at the issuer-admin freeze layer.

Pre-Merge era (Ethereum Merge ~2022-09-15 is ~8 years downstream);
no PBS / relay-filter primitive exists in 2014. not_applicable on
construct-did-not-exist grounds.

Circle USDC Blacklisted() transaction for Cryptex ETH address 0x0931cA... executed
2024-09-27 03:00 UTC (tx 0xa10d4e1a...ffd8da). On-chain receipt is the primary anchor;
usdtbanlist community tracker confirms the freeze state for the address.

XMR/ZEC/DASH are independent base-chain assets (no issuer/contract);
Bittrex cannot freeze them on-chain. The action is an offramp
market removal, not an asset-onchain freeze.

Wahrstätter data covers 2024-02-20. Slice [2024-02-06, 2024-03-05]: pre 53.13% ± 2.40,
event day 48.75%, post 50.39% ± 1.47. Small downward movement but within 2 sd of pre-mean;
null shape.

The NRB notice is an FX-control-law prohibition, not an ISP/DNS network block;
no replayable OONI / Censored Planet / Cloudflare Radar measurement is captured
(per codebook §1.5, no L0 observation can be admitted without one).

dydx.exchange and trade.dydx.exchange remained reachable globally;
the restriction is account-level platform-block logic invoked by
a compliance-vendor flag, not a DNS or ISP-level block.

The six assets are independent base-chain tokens (no issuer/contract);
Upbit cannot freeze them on-chain. The action is an off-ramp market
removal, not an asset-onchain freeze.

No issuer-level asset freeze invoked by Aave's frontend policy;
the sibling asset-layer action (Circle USDC blacklist) is
captured in circle-usdc-tornado-2022.

No SDN listing or stablecoin-issuer freeze primitive applicable;
KuCoin's Canada exit operates at the platform-service layer,
not at the issuer-admin freeze layer.

MetaMask is a self-custody wallet, not a centralized-exchange off-ramp;
the load-bearing restriction is the in-wallet swap/staking frontend
surface (l4_frontend).

Per CZ's clarification, the Binance Chain DEX blockchain was NOT blocked;
only the binance.org web interface restricted access. No consensus
surface engaged.

No frontend claim is retained for this row. The retained observation
is the legal/off-ramp severance of a designated virtual-currency MSB;
no operator-controlled UI surface is identified or measured here.

No blockchain RPC layer in scope. The MEV-Boost / Flashbots
Protect public-RPC compliance substrate did not exist in 2012;
not_applicable on construct-did-not-exist grounds.

Garantex's website went to maintenance as a consequence of the
freeze, but this is not an externally-imposed L4 domain/UI block;
the load-bearing effect is the offramp/service suspension.

mtgox.com continued to serve trading-platform pages through May 2013;
no frontend takedown or domain seizure was associated with the
2013-05-14 fiat-rail action. Frontend-enforcement layer not implicated.

FATF R.15 INR does not mandate on-chain asset-level blacklisting;
the standard governs VASP metadata-handling obligations rather
than the underlying asset.

mtgox.com was already offline from the February 2014 bankruptcy;
the 2015-08-01 arrest did not produce a separate frontend
enforcement event.
